WEBVTT

00:00.567 --> 00:03.987
<b>III</b>

00:00.567 --> 00:03.987
<b><i>Mushoku Tensei</i></b>

00:00.567 --> 00:03.987
<b><b><i>Jobless Reincarnation</i></b></b>

00:30.147 --> 00:32.117
<i>I beheld a deity.</i>

00:39.017 --> 00:42.657
<i>A deity in repose, like the Buddha.</i>

00:42.657 --> 00:46.367
<i>A sacred personage, 
to whom I must show no disrespect.</i>

00:55.777 --> 00:57.687
<i>Her waist does not curve.</i>

00:57.687 --> 01:00.327
<i>Her physique makes one wonder 
if she might be too young.</i>

01:00.777 --> 01:04.137
<i>Could that be a sacred 
urna there on her chest?</i>

01:05.797 --> 01:07.307
It's chilly.

01:09.897 --> 01:11.937
<i>We've both been through a lot,</i>

01:11.937 --> 01:15.087
<i>but I'm glad to be married 
to Roxy like this.</i>

01:15.537 --> 01:16.727
<i>Whoops.</i>

01:16.727 --> 01:19.307
<i>Time's tight in the mornings. 
We've got to get up.</i>

01:19.947 --> 01:22.857
Roxy, wake up. It's morning.

01:27.677 --> 01:29.767
Good morning.

01:31.287 --> 01:33.667
Good morning.

01:34.967 --> 01:38.547
What are you looking so disappointed for?

01:38.547 --> 01:44.387
Oh, I just wished I could take a 
good look at you in a better light.

01:46.177 --> 01:47.307
Honestly.

01:47.307 --> 01:50.727
We need to hurry. 
Everyone else must be up by now.

01:52.987 --> 01:54.187
Right!

02:02.007 --> 02:03.517
Morning, Sylphie.

02:03.907 --> 02:05.497
Morning, Rudy.

02:06.827 --> 02:09.117
Lucie is doing well as ever.

02:09.117 --> 02:11.257
Morning, Lucie.

02:11.257 --> 02:13.827
<i>Despite all my worrying,</i>

02:13.827 --> 02:16.287
<i>Lucie is growing fast.</i>

02:16.657 --> 02:18.577
<i>And Sylphie's been well 
since giving birth.</i>

02:18.577 --> 02:20.287
<i>They're both the picture of health.</i>

02:20.557 --> 02:22.797
Our little girl is cute as ever.

02:22.797 --> 02:26.677
She sure is. I wonder how 
she can be so adorable.

02:26.677 --> 02:28.887
Because her mommy's 
just as cute, I'll bet.

02:29.257 --> 02:30.637
Oh, you.

02:30.637 --> 02:32.387
Thanks, Rudy.

02:35.747 --> 02:37.357
Morning, Roxy.

02:37.937 --> 02:41.517
G-Good morning.

02:42.107 --> 02:44.177
Um... Roxy,

02:44.177 --> 02:46.207
how was Rudy last night?

02:46.207 --> 02:50.127
Oh, uh, well, he was good to me.

02:50.127 --> 02:52.137
Rudy was gentle, and—

02:52.137 --> 02:54.027
I'm, um, sorry.

02:54.027 --> 02:56.117
You've got nothing to apologize for.

02:56.117 --> 02:57.597
You think so?

02:57.597 --> 02:58.857
I do.

03:01.967 --> 03:03.457
Morning, Norn.

03:03.457 --> 03:05.457
Good morning, Brother.

03:05.697 --> 03:09.387
I wrote up a little more 
of Ruijerd's story.

03:09.387 --> 03:11.167
Would you mind reading it over?

03:11.167 --> 03:12.297
Of course.

03:12.787 --> 03:17.677
<i>I planned to make a book 
to clear the Superds' name,</i>

03:17.677 --> 03:19.807
<i>but Norn's mostly taken over writing it.</i>

03:20.137 --> 03:23.677
<i>She's still learning, but I can 
tell she's trying her best,</i>

03:23.947 --> 03:27.057
<i>so I bet she'll turn out a 
better story than I could.</i>

03:27.617 --> 03:29.247
I'm looking forward to it.

03:33.547 --> 03:35.437
Morning, Mom.

03:36.437 --> 03:38.827
Mom, it's Rudeus.

03:45.207 --> 03:49.167
<i>It's been months since 
we returned to Sharia,</i>

03:49.167 --> 03:51.107
<i>but Zenith's memory hasn't returned.</i>

03:51.587 --> 03:56.607
<i>She is changing little by little, 
but all I can do for now is wait and see.</i>

03:58.097 --> 04:01.057
Breakfast! Breakfast!

04:01.057 --> 04:03.567
Breakfast is served!

04:06.037 --> 04:09.097
Good morning, Big Brother, my lady.

04:09.097 --> 04:10.687
Morning, Aisha.

04:10.687 --> 04:12.847
What's for breakfast today?

04:12.847 --> 04:16.637
It's pretty much the same as usual!

04:16.637 --> 04:17.947
Aisha.

04:18.177 --> 04:22.227
Stop being difficult and 
tell him what we're having.

04:22.607 --> 04:27.817
Yoco bean and tuber soup and wheat 
bread with nourishing mare's milk!

04:28.277 --> 04:33.447
Master Rudeus, Madam Sylphiette, 
Madam Roxy, good morning.

04:33.447 --> 04:35.467
Good morning, Lilia.

04:35.807 --> 04:41.427
<i>Aisha and Lilia are running the house 
as our maids, the same as ever.</i>

04:36.147 --> 04:39.887
Now, Aisha, we must serve the 
food before it gets cold.

04:39.887 --> 04:41.147
Sure thing!

04:41.427 --> 04:44.687
Breakfast! Breakfast! Breakfast is served!

04:41.427 --> 04:47.677
<i>Aisha's a handful, and Lilia scolds 
her a lot, but they both seem happy.</i>

04:43.387 --> 04:45.937
Aisha! Take this seriously!

04:48.497 --> 04:50.947
<i>We were scattered all over the world,</i>

04:50.947 --> 04:54.197
<i>but managed to come 
together as a family again.</i>

04:54.577 --> 04:57.287
<i>That's enough to make me happy now.</i>

04:57.787 --> 05:00.277
Well then, let's dig in.

05:14.167 --> 05:17.497
<i>Sylphie and I are going 
back to school today.</i>

05:17.957 --> 05:20.337
<i>And we're not the only ones.</i>

05:22.007 --> 05:23.757
Is something wrong?

05:23.757 --> 05:25.707
No, nothing at all.

05:25.707 --> 05:26.977
Are you sure?

05:26.977 --> 05:31.407
Say, have you already introduced 
Roxy to everyone at school?

05:31.407 --> 05:32.267
Yes.

05:32.577 --> 05:36.467
When I recommended Master Roxy 
to the university as an instructor,

05:36.467 --> 05:40.517
I told everyone how wonderful she 
was while I showed her around campus!

05:40.517 --> 05:45.087
She's such a sublime person that 
learning about her lofty nature

05:45.087 --> 05:48.257
could only ever be a plus to 
them all in whatever they do!

05:49.397 --> 05:51.027
That's so like you.

05:52.807 --> 05:56.767
I appreciate you introducing 
me to so many people, Rudy,

05:56.767 --> 06:02.517
but you always told them I was your 
"master" and never that I'm your "wife."

06:03.967 --> 06:05.377
Rudy?

06:05.377 --> 06:07.857
I... I'm so sorry, Roxy.

06:07.857 --> 06:10.707
Oh, my sweetheart.

06:10.707 --> 06:12.927
But I really do love you.

06:14.017 --> 06:16.697
Th-Thank you very much.

06:16.697 --> 06:20.047
Hey, Rudy, don't you have 
anything to say to <i>me?</i>

06:20.487 --> 06:23.147
Of course I love you, too, Sylphie.

06:23.147 --> 06:24.527
I love...

06:26.167 --> 06:28.037
both of you!

06:29.917 --> 06:31.637
That's the spirit, Quagmire!

06:30.167 --> 06:31.137
H-Hey!

06:31.137 --> 06:32.237
Rudy?!

06:31.637 --> 06:33.427
That's our boss!

06:32.237 --> 06:34.407
No more stunts like that at school.

06:33.427 --> 06:35.707
I'm jealous, you lucky bastard!

06:34.407 --> 06:35.667
Definitely not.

06:35.667 --> 06:38.277
Brother, you're embarrassing me.

06:43.167 --> 06:45.907
Bye, then. I'm going this way.

06:45.907 --> 06:48.297
Sure. Good luck with your lessons.

06:48.297 --> 06:49.187
Thank you.

06:51.127 --> 06:54.187
Brother, I'm coming home again today.

06:58.777 --> 06:59.857
Morning.

06:59.857 --> 07:01.137
What took you so long?

07:01.137 --> 07:02.037
Morning.

07:02.037 --> 07:03.617
Morning, Norn.

07:03.617 --> 07:06.317
Norn is popular, I see.

07:06.317 --> 07:08.227
She is cute.

07:08.227 --> 07:11.287
It's because everyone can 
tell how hard she's working.

07:11.287 --> 07:13.247
It makes you want to root for her.

07:13.247 --> 07:16.167
<i>As her brother, I'm glad she's popular,</i>

07:16.487 --> 07:20.887
<i>but if any of those guys try anything 
with Norn, I'll make them regret it.</i>

07:21.257 --> 07:25.977
<i>There's no way I'll let some 
shady stranger have my little sister.</i>

07:21.257 --> 07:23.477
We should go shopping in town sometime.

07:23.477 --> 07:25.977
Hey! Norn's going with <i>us!</i>

07:26.327 --> 07:28.137
<i>Right, Dad?</i>

07:27.057 --> 07:29.167
Let's all go together, then.

07:35.177 --> 07:36.277
Come in.

07:37.167 --> 07:38.597
Pardon us.

07:41.207 --> 07:43.347
P-Pardon us.

07:44.197 --> 07:46.107
I've been expecting you.

07:47.257 --> 07:50.437
Rudeus, you'll be returning 
to your studies today?

07:50.437 --> 07:55.407
Yes. The other day was only a greeting, 
but I'll be under your tutelage again.

07:55.407 --> 07:58.337
We're glad to have you back.

07:59.387 --> 08:03.497
And Roxy, this will be your 
first day teaching here.

08:03.497 --> 08:05.057
Are you nervous?

08:05.357 --> 08:06.267
Yes...

08:08.297 --> 08:09.297
Master.

08:10.877 --> 08:16.557
How you've changed. What happened to the 
Roxy who said she needed no teacher?

08:16.557 --> 08:19.697
True. I'm surprised myself.

08:19.697 --> 08:22.537
I was full of myself back then.

08:22.537 --> 08:28.447
But now, I think I can understand a 
little of the joys of teaching others.

08:30.727 --> 08:34.087
We're glad to have you, Instructor Roxy.

08:34.407 --> 08:35.427
Thank you!

08:37.357 --> 08:40.327
Well then, I'll go to class ahead of you.

08:40.327 --> 08:42.367
All right. See you later.

08:45.687 --> 08:47.367
Good morning.

08:48.207 --> 08:50.627
Huh... Guess I'm the first one here.

08:50.627 --> 08:52.127
Oh, boss.

08:52.837 --> 08:54.797
Good meowning.

08:54.797 --> 08:56.267
Morning.

08:56.267 --> 08:57.757
Morning, you two.

08:58.177 --> 09:00.157
We were watching mew, boss.

09:00.467 --> 09:04.617
Must be nice, showing up to 
school with two women in tow.

09:04.617 --> 09:08.797
How could you ditch us and 
bring home your second? Nuhni.

09:08.797 --> 09:12.657
We graduate this year, so we're 
gonna find someone, meow.

09:12.657 --> 09:15.417
That's right. This year, we duel.

09:15.677 --> 09:18.147
We'll find ourselves men to take home.

09:18.147 --> 09:20.397
I'll find myself a good one, meow!

09:20.397 --> 09:24.007
<i>They've always acted like they 
didn't have time for romance,</i>

09:24.007 --> 09:27.927
<i>but I guess seeing me with a beauty 
on each arm has them jealous.</i>

09:27.927 --> 09:29.187
Master!

09:29.187 --> 09:32.817
Master, it's you! Good morning.

09:32.817 --> 09:35.667
Good morning, Grand Master.

09:35.667 --> 09:37.257
Morning, Zanoba.

09:37.607 --> 09:39.187
You, too, Julie. Morning.

09:39.187 --> 09:42.457
Since you're in the classroom, 
will you be rejoining us?

09:42.457 --> 09:45.157
Yeah. We can do more research together.

09:45.157 --> 09:47.077
That's perfect, then.

09:47.077 --> 09:49.867
I have something I'd like 
you to look at later.

09:49.867 --> 09:51.467
You have something new?

09:53.357 --> 09:56.867
Only the fruits of the 
past six months' research!

09:58.147 --> 10:01.187
A-All right. I can hardly wait.

10:09.937 --> 10:11.217
Morning.

10:11.727 --> 10:13.017
Morning.

10:14.257 --> 10:15.477
Are you okay?

10:15.987 --> 10:17.617
I'm fine.

10:17.617 --> 10:20.367
Anyway, since you're back at school,

10:20.367 --> 10:22.737
I assume you won't be going 
anywhere for a while.

10:22.737 --> 10:23.717
Nope.

10:24.257 --> 10:25.257
Good.

10:25.827 --> 10:28.417
I can continue my experiments, then.

10:29.077 --> 10:30.487
Rudeus!

10:30.727 --> 10:33.387
Cliff. Good morning.

10:33.387 --> 10:36.587
Lise told me that you came back with her,

10:36.587 --> 10:40.047
but would it have killed 
you to come say hello?

10:40.047 --> 10:41.547
Sorry.

10:41.547 --> 10:43.867
I did drop by, but...

10:44.147 --> 10:46.997
you seemed busy with Elinalise.

10:47.947 --> 10:49.637
I... I see.

10:49.637 --> 10:52.137
Well, I can't blame you for that, then.

10:52.137 --> 10:53.807
It was partly my fault.

10:54.147 --> 10:59.257
Still, you could have come to 
tell me your child was born.

10:59.257 --> 11:01.177
Th-That's fair.

11:01.177 --> 11:03.727
I'm sure the baby's keeping you busy,

11:03.727 --> 11:06.947
but I'd almost think 
you've been avoiding me lately.

11:07.207 --> 11:09.367
<i>Maybe I have been.</i>

11:09.367 --> 11:11.407
<i>He's a follower of Millis,</i>

11:11.407 --> 11:15.937
<i>so I did figure he'd hassle 
me for having two wives.</i>

11:15.937 --> 11:19.927
Or is there some reason 
you didn't want to see me?

11:24.107 --> 11:24.957
The thing is,

11:24.957 --> 11:26.227
I've taken a second—

11:24.957 --> 11:26.667
Good morning.

11:27.627 --> 11:30.137
Now, take your seats.

11:31.297 --> 11:33.847
I am Roxy Migurdia Greyrat.

11:34.367 --> 11:39.467
As of today, she will be teaching 
at the Ranoa University of Magic.

11:39.467 --> 11:45.857
I will assist her at first, but she 
will be your class's new advisor,

11:45.857 --> 11:48.447
so I hope you will all 
be on your best behavior.

11:49.247 --> 11:52.567
I believe I've already been 
introduced to many of you,

11:52.567 --> 11:57.147
but I am the second wife 
of Rudeus Greyrat there.

11:57.147 --> 12:01.107
No doubt we will be on different 
terms as teacher and students,

12:01.107 --> 12:02.867
but I look forward to getting to know you.

12:03.427 --> 12:05.237
Well, now...

12:05.537 --> 12:08.407
Your <i>second</i> wife?

12:20.967 --> 12:24.977
Rudeus, is being faithful 
completely beyond you?

12:24.977 --> 12:29.647
Yes. I do think I could have 
been a little better at it.

12:31.487 --> 12:36.907
I blessed you that day because you said 
you'd love Sylphie alone, you know?

12:36.907 --> 12:41.827
I know, and I'm deeply grateful 
for your kind words then.

12:41.827 --> 12:47.787
I know you're not a follower of Millis, 
of course, so I'll leave it at that.

12:48.207 --> 12:50.677
In fact, I'll celebrate.

12:52.087 --> 12:53.857
Congratulations.

12:53.857 --> 12:55.707
Thank you very much.

13:00.697 --> 13:04.337
I see your sister at the 
church in town sometimes.

13:05.967 --> 13:10.907
She told me she wanted 
to have a happy marriage

13:10.907 --> 13:13.597
like you and Sylphie someday.

13:14.347 --> 13:18.867
What did she say to you when 
you brought a second wife home?

13:20.587 --> 13:22.327
She was furious.

13:22.327 --> 13:24.077
I'll bet she was!

13:24.077 --> 13:28.237
She prayed for your and your father's 
safe return almost every day.

13:28.237 --> 13:33.117
I'm sure she was delighted 
that you did come home alive.

13:33.627 --> 13:38.327
But now that she's lost her father, 
you're all she has left.

13:38.887 --> 13:42.527
Don't you think you should give 
more thought to how Norn feels?

13:43.137 --> 13:44.377
I do.

13:44.957 --> 13:49.097
It isn't good to have <i>too</i> many spouses.

13:49.097 --> 13:50.497
Right.

13:50.987 --> 13:53.007
So, um, Cliff...

13:53.007 --> 13:54.927
Yes, Rudeus?

13:54.927 --> 13:59.277
You've been keeping an eye on 
Norn for me, huh? Thank you.

14:00.587 --> 14:04.047
I only gave her someone to talk 
to since I spotted her in church.

14:04.047 --> 14:06.517
Oh, and another thing.

14:06.517 --> 14:09.367
You shouldn't let a girl her age 
walk around town alone.

14:09.637 --> 14:14.717
This is a safe neighborhood, but there 
are kidnappers in the backstreets.

14:14.717 --> 14:17.137
True. I'll take that to heart.

14:17.137 --> 14:19.397
Will you really? You're always—

14:19.397 --> 14:22.317
Now, now. Why don't you leave it at that?

14:22.317 --> 14:25.147
After all, he has come 
back to us alive and well.

14:26.277 --> 14:29.637
Well, he does seem repentant.

14:29.637 --> 14:32.117
I'll forgive you your sins.

14:32.117 --> 14:35.567
Great Millis is magnanimous.

14:35.567 --> 14:37.257
I appreciate it.

14:41.757 --> 14:43.807
Lise told me the story,

14:43.807 --> 14:46.857
but was the thing that took your 
hand really that dangerous?

14:48.177 --> 14:50.497
It was a hydra that 
magic had no effect on.

14:50.497 --> 14:52.367
It was immune to magic?

14:52.827 --> 14:55.347
I can understand why you struggled, then.

14:55.777 --> 14:57.377
I'm amazed you beat it.

14:57.377 --> 14:59.657
Only thanks to my dad.

15:00.287 --> 15:04.487
We did win, but we lost a lot, too.

15:08.527 --> 15:11.427
Master, please wait a moment.

15:15.307 --> 15:17.477
Look at this.

15:17.477 --> 15:19.147
What is it?

15:19.147 --> 15:21.737
The thing I mentioned 
to you in the classroom.

15:21.737 --> 15:23.747
The fruits of our research.

15:23.747 --> 15:25.787
Now, hold out your left arm.

15:25.787 --> 15:26.987
S-Sure.

15:34.217 --> 15:36.027
Won't it fall off?

15:36.027 --> 15:39.627
The incantation is 
"O Earth, become my arm."

15:39.627 --> 15:40.647
Pardon?

15:40.647 --> 15:42.927
Go ahead. Recite it.

15:44.237 --> 15:47.067
"O Earth, become my arm."

15:56.157 --> 15:58.157
Wh-Whoa!

15:58.157 --> 16:00.457
It moves! It moves!

16:00.457 --> 16:02.097
Here, Rudeus.

16:05.357 --> 16:08.787
Amazing! I can even feel the fingertips!

16:08.787 --> 16:09.997
What is this thing?

16:09.997 --> 16:13.757
A magical implement that 
moves as you will it to!

16:13.757 --> 16:15.827
While analyzing the automaton,

16:15.827 --> 16:19.617
I turned to Cliff for assistance, 
and we managed to reach this point!

16:19.617 --> 16:24.697
With it, I can restrain my freakish 
strength and sculpt figurines.

16:24.697 --> 16:26.547
That's incredible!

16:26.547 --> 16:30.517
If you <i>want</i> force, it gets stronger 
the more mana you feed it.

16:30.937 --> 16:32.257
Oh?

16:36.137 --> 16:38.907
You're angry about what 
I said earlier, aren't you?!

16:38.907 --> 16:44.487
We didn't know if you could operate it 
with a missing hand, but it seems fine.

16:44.487 --> 16:48.217
Hey, can I do magic with this hand?

16:49.187 --> 16:51.727
Would you let go of me already—

16:51.727 --> 16:54.147
Well, shall we experiment?

16:53.037 --> 16:54.147
Don't grip tighter!

16:59.617 --> 17:00.947
What's that?

17:00.947 --> 17:02.447
Another duel, maybe?

17:02.447 --> 17:03.127
Really?

17:07.657 --> 17:10.057
All ready!

17:10.057 --> 17:12.197
Okay. Give it a try.

17:12.847 --> 17:14.517
Here goes.

17:44.037 --> 17:47.557
It looks like you can cast spells 
while wearing it without an issue.

17:47.557 --> 17:48.437
Yes.

17:50.157 --> 17:52.767
Magnificent, Master!
You never disappoint!

17:52.767 --> 17:56.217
This is one hell of an invention. 
Honestly, I'm floored.

17:56.217 --> 17:57.887
Thank you!

17:57.887 --> 18:01.367
I would gladly give you 
that hand, if you wish.

18:01.927 --> 18:03.007
You mean it?

18:03.007 --> 18:07.447
Yes. It's only a prototype, 
but it should be better than nothing.

18:07.447 --> 18:14.447
And with you and Cliff to help me, 
I can make a similar piece in no time.

18:14.447 --> 18:17.787
Speaking of which, does this 
magical implement have a name?

18:18.457 --> 18:21.407
We haven't given it one yet.

18:21.407 --> 18:26.427
Neither Cliff nor I have much 
talent for naming things.

18:26.427 --> 18:29.667
Since you're here, 
would you name it for us?

18:29.667 --> 18:32.507
Oh, yes. Please do.

18:40.517 --> 18:45.277
In that case, I'll take from both your 
names and call it the "Hand of Zaliff."

18:45.597 --> 18:48.157
You left out your own name.

18:48.157 --> 18:51.247
That's fine. I didn't help make it.

18:51.247 --> 18:54.797
I would hardly say that
 you played no part...

18:58.567 --> 18:59.817
But very well.

18:59.817 --> 19:00.667
In that case,

19:00.667 --> 19:04.847
that hand is the Hand of Zaliff, 
prototype number one.

19:23.737 --> 19:27.157
Welcome home, Big Brother!

19:30.837 --> 19:33.827
Would you like dinner? A bath?

19:33.827 --> 19:35.667
Or maybe...

19:35.667 --> 19:38.867
little... old... me?

19:40.197 --> 19:44.317
In that case... I think I'll have you!

19:44.317 --> 19:46.677
Cootchie-cootchie-coo!

19:46.227 --> 19:48.757
Big Brother's attacking me!

19:48.757 --> 19:49.787
Huh?

19:54.107 --> 19:55.417
I'm home.

20:00.717 --> 20:03.507
Is that prosthetic hand 
a magical implement?

20:03.507 --> 20:07.497
Yes. It's the fruit of Zanoba 
and Cliff's research.

20:07.497 --> 20:11.207
That amazing. It moves like a real hand.

20:11.207 --> 20:15.427
This range of motion should be enough 
to get through everyday life.

20:15.427 --> 20:16.837
And...

20:16.837 --> 20:20.197
I can have my fill of both of you!

20:20.497 --> 20:22.047
Really, Rudy.

20:22.047 --> 20:24.217
Hey! Where do you think you're touching?

20:24.217 --> 20:26.837
Brother, you're embarrassing me.

20:26.837 --> 20:33.167
Dinner! Dinner! Dinner is served!

20:34.217 --> 20:37.847
Today's menu is pretty 
much the same as usual.

20:37.847 --> 20:39.247
Aisha!

20:39.247 --> 20:40.757
I know.

20:41.307 --> 20:43.007
Thank you for this meal.

20:43.987 --> 20:49.027
<i>So much has happened since the 
mass teleportation in Fittoa.</i>

20:49.497 --> 20:53.097
<i>Adventuring on the Demon Continent, 
parting ways with Eris,</i>

20:53.547 --> 20:56.997
<i>curing my condition, marrying Sylphie,</i>

20:57.417 --> 21:01.037
<i>reuniting with Roxy, rescuing Mom...</i>

21:01.697 --> 21:05.087
<i>I've lost things along the way,</i>

21:05.587 --> 21:07.847
<i>but I've gotten back to regular old life.</i>

21:08.787 --> 21:12.557
<i>I'm going to keep on 
treasuring this "normal."</i>

21:48.317 --> 21:51.377
<i>I've gotten my peaceful life back,</i>

21:56.327 --> 21:59.947
<i>so here I am again, praying silently.</i>

22:02.007 --> 22:05.007
<b>Episode 3
Life Back at Home</b>

23:35.017 --> 23:40.097
Next Time
A King-Class Water Mage
